WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:01.680
Welcome.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:08.510
My name is Samuel Nixon Jr., an
alum of the MIT Gospel Choir.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.000
Did you know that
Black students at MIT

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.190
have traditionally
relied on faith and music

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:20.210
for spiritual sustenance
through the academic and social

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:23.630
pressures of life
at the Institute?

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:24.980
Yeah.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:30.470
The MIT Gospel Choir is a
half century year old example

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.160
of this tradition and
meaningful reliance.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:41.320
And from its early
formation in 1971 by others,

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.500
this body of
faithful students has

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:50.610
grown from the informal original
group of 10 undergraduates who

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:56.680
quote, unquote, "simply
enjoyed singing to each other,"

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.970
according to the then president
and co-director Ricardo Hall,

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:05.860
"to a more formal and
amazing group of songsters,

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.350
all walks of life."

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:13.390
Choir members have been singing
traditional gospel, hymns,

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:19.330
and spirituals for around five
decades in local churches,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:23.080
in the Christian Fellowship
services at the MIT Chapel

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:25.570
and all around the
Boston/Cambridge area

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.430
and beyond.

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:33.500
Today, during this holy season,
a segment of the MIT Gospel

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:36.410
Choir alums from
across the years,

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:41.180
I'm privileged to present to
you just a few moments of joy

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:45.200
and celebration of some of the
historic journey of this legacy

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.080
choir.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:53.410
Won't you pause with us now to
remember some of the singing

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:56.980
fellowship and exciting
moments of sharing the gospel

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:02.700
and song in this special
MIT Gospel Choir holiday

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.760
presentation?

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:08.449
It's our joy to share with
you with each musical note

00:02:08.449 --> 00:02:13.720
and chord amidst the hustle
and bustle of the season.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:14.560
Yeah, we know.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:15.870
We know.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:20.490
Come, relax, and spend
a few moments with us

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:23.580
as you hear the
sweetness of song,

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:26.310
the melodies of
memorable moments,

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:32.760
and voices of faith expressed
during our student years.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:38.730
Yes, even around the
corridors of the Massachusetts

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.720
Institute of Technology.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:44.566
Welcome.

00:02:44.566 --> 00:02:49.012
