00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:28.510
[APPLAUSE]

00:22:28.510 --> 00:22:32.110
I was contacted sometime
during the summer

00:22:32.110 --> 00:22:36.430
preceding my freshman
year by a student

00:22:36.430 --> 00:22:39.850
at MIT, Georgette
Redmond, who was also

00:22:39.850 --> 00:22:41.620
from Ohio, Toledo, Ohio.

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:44.260
And she called to contact me.

00:22:44.260 --> 00:22:51.820
And we shared some information
about our mutual interest

00:22:51.820 --> 00:22:52.540
in singing.

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:57.610
I was elated to find out that
there was such an organization.

00:22:57.610 --> 00:22:59.800
But it turned out to be
extremely important to me.

00:22:59.800 --> 00:23:02.320
Later that same
summer, I tragically

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:04.390
lost my younger brother.

00:23:04.390 --> 00:23:10.210
And the choir was a
huge part of the support

00:23:10.210 --> 00:23:14.980
that I received while
grieving, but also needing

00:23:14.980 --> 00:23:17.650
to maintain my
studies and maintain

00:23:17.650 --> 00:23:19.240
most importantly, my faith.

00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:22.360
I think we impacted
MIT and the community

00:23:22.360 --> 00:23:29.170
by demonstrating our faith,
adding a different perspective

00:23:29.170 --> 00:23:35.800
to the faith community at
MIT from an African-American

00:23:35.800 --> 00:23:41.830
perspective and an artistic
perspective as well.

00:23:41.830 --> 00:23:45.640
How did I come to participate
in the MIT Gospel Choir?

00:23:45.640 --> 00:23:47.770
Well, I had a couple
of friends approach me.

00:23:47.770 --> 00:23:50.470
And one at a time,
they were like, Sean,

00:23:50.470 --> 00:23:52.780
we'd like you to
join a gospel choir.

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:55.800
I said, I'm Catholic.

00:23:55.800 --> 00:23:59.280
We don't really
do gospel choirs.

00:23:59.280 --> 00:23:59.940
I'm not sure.

00:23:59.940 --> 00:24:01.830
I'm already in the
Catholic community.

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:05.400
Didn't know who would be
a conflict of interest.

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:09.510
And thirdly, I
really can't sing.

00:24:09.510 --> 00:24:13.660
And one by one, they each said
that those were not issues.

00:24:13.660 --> 00:24:15.020
There were not conflicts.

00:24:15.020 --> 00:24:16.270
And I said, I'd give it a try.

00:24:16.270 --> 00:24:19.030
And I'm glad they persisted,
because I really enjoyed it.

00:24:19.030 --> 00:24:21.690
It was great to see so many
people from different walks

00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:24.510
of life, from the
North to South,

00:24:24.510 --> 00:24:27.780
from the urban settings,
the rural settings,

00:24:27.780 --> 00:24:30.210
different denominations
get together and just

00:24:30.210 --> 00:24:32.730
praise the Lord together.

00:24:32.730 --> 00:24:36.600
The experience was great,
especially in a very high

00:24:36.600 --> 00:24:39.690
stress environment.

00:24:39.690 --> 00:24:43.890
It was always time well spent
when I went to the practices

00:24:43.890 --> 00:24:45.510
with the MIT Gospel Choir.

00:24:45.510 --> 00:24:48.720
One day, I invited my
parents and my brother

00:24:48.720 --> 00:24:51.940
down to see us perform.

00:24:51.940 --> 00:24:54.540
It was the first time
we had a full band.

00:24:54.540 --> 00:24:58.380
We had a couple
guitarists, organists.

00:24:58.380 --> 00:25:01.290
And I didn't tell
them that I was

00:25:01.290 --> 00:25:05.130
going to be conducting a
couple of songs with the choir.

00:25:05.130 --> 00:25:06.360
Turned out really well.

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:07.650
Totally surprised them.

00:25:07.650 --> 00:25:12.210
I think my brother even asked
if I had switched religions,

00:25:12.210 --> 00:25:13.260
which I didn't.

00:25:13.260 --> 00:25:16.830
But it was very memorable.

00:25:16.830 --> 00:25:18.976
And I'm glad they came.

00:25:18.976 --> 00:25:22.760
