00:27:10.250 --> 00:27:11.540
Hi, I'm Cheryll Gill.

00:27:11.540 --> 00:27:15.360
I joined the MIT Gospel
Choir in the fall of 1988,

00:27:15.360 --> 00:27:16.822
which was my freshman year.

00:27:16.822 --> 00:27:18.530
I was happy to join
the choir, because it

00:27:18.530 --> 00:27:22.850
was a continuation of
my experiences in church

00:27:22.850 --> 00:27:25.610
and community choir
since my youth.

00:27:25.610 --> 00:27:28.910
I really appreciated
the fellowship time

00:27:28.910 --> 00:27:30.800
with the Gospel Choir.

00:27:30.800 --> 00:27:35.030
We encouraged each other as we
practiced songs in rehearsal.

00:27:35.030 --> 00:27:38.840
And I count several
lifelong friendships

00:27:38.840 --> 00:27:41.420
among the choir members.

00:27:41.420 --> 00:27:45.170
Our choir engagements were
also an outreach ministry.

00:27:45.170 --> 00:27:48.260
I recall singing at college
Sundays at the Massachusetts

00:27:48.260 --> 00:27:53.030
Avenue Baptist Church in
Cambridge and other area

00:27:53.030 --> 00:27:54.140
colleges.

00:27:54.140 --> 00:27:58.040
But I think my favorite
memory was the spring 1989

00:27:58.040 --> 00:28:00.410
concert with Candace
Buckner singing

00:28:00.410 --> 00:28:05.960
God Is to a large audience
in Kresge Auditorium.

00:28:05.960 --> 00:28:08.390
Our concerts gave
us an opportunity

00:28:08.390 --> 00:28:13.589
to reach people who didn't
come from a faith tradition.

00:28:13.589 --> 00:28:18.026
[MUSIC - TYE TRIBBETT,
 "HALLELUJAH TO YOUR NAME"]

00:28:33.309 --> 00:28:37.290
(SINGING) Lord, You
are good and your mercy

00:28:37.290 --> 00:28:41.058
endureth forever and ever.

00:28:41.058 --> 00:28:45.348
Your power is greater
than anything.

00:28:49.614 --> 00:28:56.600
Because of Your grace I have
life everlasting and more

00:28:56.600 --> 00:28:57.550
abundantly.

00:28:57.550 --> 00:29:02.000
Lord, you mean everything.

00:29:04.970 --> 00:29:12.470
Lord, and I worship
You most high.

00:29:12.470 --> 00:29:19.970
And I'll bless Your name O God.

00:29:19.970 --> 00:29:28.470
For You are worthy of
the highest praise.

00:29:28.470 --> 00:29:33.470
Hallelujah to Your name.

00:29:41.970 --> 00:29:44.160
Thank you for taking
the time to share

00:29:44.160 --> 00:29:46.500
in this inaugural
special presentation

00:29:46.500 --> 00:29:50.010
by the MIT Gospel Choir alums
during the holiday season

00:29:50.010 --> 00:29:51.690
of 2022.

00:29:51.690 --> 00:29:55.380
We hope that you found it
enriching, encouraging,

00:29:55.380 --> 00:29:59.370
and even exciting as we reveal
just a glimpse of the history

00:29:59.370 --> 00:30:03.450
of over a half a century that
this organization has been

00:30:03.450 --> 00:30:08.700
offering songs of hope and help
and healing to a hurting world.

00:30:08.700 --> 00:30:10.980
The MIT Gospel
Choir is a witness

00:30:10.980 --> 00:30:12.690
of what has been
a significant part

00:30:12.690 --> 00:30:16.050
of our life-changing
experiences while engaged

00:30:16.050 --> 00:30:19.170
in our academic studies at MIT.

00:30:19.170 --> 00:30:21.150
As you've just heard
and experienced

00:30:21.150 --> 00:30:24.480
in the music, testimonials,
and songs of just a few

00:30:24.480 --> 00:30:27.270
of the alums in
our group, you can

00:30:27.270 --> 00:30:30.510
tell that this organization
has been a blessing to many,

00:30:30.510 --> 00:30:32.980
not just those in
the MIT community,

00:30:32.980 --> 00:30:35.580
but also across the
greater Boston/Cambridge

00:30:35.580 --> 00:30:39.840
area and even the Eastern
coast of the United States.

00:30:39.840 --> 00:30:42.390
We are grateful to
have made a difference

00:30:42.390 --> 00:30:44.370
in the lives of the
people whom we've

00:30:44.370 --> 00:30:47.580
touched through song and
witness and our service

00:30:47.580 --> 00:30:48.810
to our community.

00:30:48.810 --> 00:30:50.670
And we'd like to
give Thanks to those

00:30:50.670 --> 00:30:53.340
who have taken the
time, such as yourself,

00:30:53.340 --> 00:30:57.840
to hear our voices speak to
the value of the relationships

00:30:57.840 --> 00:31:01.620
and the fellowship that we've
experienced in our faith

00:31:01.620 --> 00:31:03.030
journeys.

00:31:03.030 --> 00:31:07.500
Many have passed our way and
still have very fond memories

00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:10.320
of the bonds and
lifelong relationships

00:31:10.320 --> 00:31:13.170
that were fostered through
the MIT Gospel Choir

00:31:13.170 --> 00:31:16.500
as it grew and developed
over the years.

00:31:16.500 --> 00:31:19.530
There is much more to
come as we look forward

00:31:19.530 --> 00:31:23.490
to presenting more of the
joyful and revealing ways

00:31:23.490 --> 00:31:25.830
that the MIT Gospel
Choir has impacted

00:31:25.830 --> 00:31:30.060
the communities of MIT
Boston/Cambridge and the East

00:31:30.060 --> 00:31:30.990
Coast.

00:31:30.990 --> 00:31:35.550
Stay tuned for our 2023
series of presentations

00:31:35.550 --> 00:31:38.340
that will be offered through
the activities of the Black

00:31:38.340 --> 00:31:44.520
Alumni of MIT, also known BAMIT,
and the MIT Alumni Association.

00:31:44.520 --> 00:31:47.640
It's an exciting time for
reunion for our choir.

00:31:47.640 --> 00:31:51.210
And we invite you to be
a special part of it.

00:31:51.210 --> 00:31:53.310
If you would more
information, you

00:31:53.310 --> 00:31:59.190
can contact Mae White
Wesson at maewesson@aol.com.

00:31:59.190 --> 00:32:06.150
That's spelled M-A-E
W-E-S-S-O-N at aol.com.

00:32:06.150 --> 00:32:11.690
Or you can also contact Samuel
Nixon Jr. at snixonj2@aol.com.

00:32:14.280 --> 00:32:21.750
That's spelled S N-I-X-O-N
J the number 2 at aol.com.

00:32:21.750 --> 00:32:24.150
We will also be
releasing announcements

00:32:24.150 --> 00:32:27.000
through the BAMIT and
MIT Alumni networks

00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:29.460
over the course of 2023.

00:32:29.460 --> 00:32:32.340
On behalf of the MIT
Gospel Choir alums,

00:32:32.340 --> 00:32:37.920
we hope you have a great rest
of your 2022 holiday experience

00:32:37.920 --> 00:32:41.280
as you reflect with us on
the songs and the testimonies

00:32:41.280 --> 00:32:42.540
you've heard.

00:32:42.540 --> 00:32:47.760
We look forward to you
joining us again in 2023.

00:32:47.760 --> 00:32:52.610
Blessings to you and your
family in this holy season.

00:32:52.610 --> 00:32:57.370
This has been a production of
